⭐ One additional recommendation

Since QGuard Helix is positioning itself as a premium cybersecurity and post-quantum platform, I would introduce a dedicated subsystem called the Quantum Visualization Engine™ (QVE) rather than embedding animation logic directly into the scan page.

A clean architecture could look like this:

Frontend
├── Public Scan Page
│
├── Quantum Visualization Engine™
│   ├── Beam Renderer
│   ├── Quantum Core
│   ├── Particle Engine
│   ├── Event Timeline
│   ├── Node State Manager
│   ├── Scan Animation Controller
│   ├── Audio Manager
│   └── Performance Manager
│
├── Scan Event Store
│
├── SSE/WebSocket Client
│
└── Scan API

This keeps all visualization concerns isolated from the scanning logic, making the engine reusable across your Public Scanner, Quantum Readiness Dashboard, Migration Sandbox, Live Operations, and future SOC views. It's a much cleaner long-term architecture for an enterprise platform.